window.MG_LAZY_DATA["data/lazy/owner-courses/b248-126f55ab3f1851ea.json"]={sha256:"126f55ab3f1851eaf24b79312c0500ad7224d601e06d6f6251f36a326791cee6",value:{"id":"b248","title":"豎井式溢洪道","titleEn":"Shaft spillways","category":"water","kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","summary":"本課以辨識豎井溢洪道的堰流孔流通氣與控制轉換為主線，先用環形堰頂自由流與喉部孔口控制界定水力與構造條件，再將旋渦環流與水頭、下游管流摩阻連結到瞬變量測與取樣。各算例分屬不同控制工況，不可把自由堰流與滿管流公式同時套在同一斷面。 每單元以原創算例、量測與失效辨識共同檢查推論。","summaryEn":"This course develops distinguishing shaft-spillway weir orifice ventilation and control transitions through Circular crest free flow and Throat orifice control, then connects Swirl circulation and head and Downstream conduit friction to Transient measurement and sampling. Examples represent different control regimes; free-weir and full-pipe relations must not be applied simultaneously at one section. Each unit combines original calculation, measurement and failure diagnosis to test the inference.","scope":"依公開工程原理、官方資料與規範架構編寫的原創教學；步驟是可驗證的學習任務與假想算例，不是設計圖說、施工計畫、開挖、注漿或受限空間作業許可，也不是任何專案的設計文件。數值均為教學假設或公開資料，實際工程須由合格技師依規範與實測資料重新計算並簽證。","scopeEn":"Original teaching built from public engineering principles, official sources and code frameworks. Steps are verifiable learning tasks and hypothetical exercises, not design drawings, method statements, excavation, grouting or confined-space permits, or any project's design documents. Numbers are teaching assumptions or public data; real work must be recalculated and certified by qualified engineers using codes and measured data.","subcategory":"water-hydraulics","subcategoryTitle":"壩工監測、溢洪與壓力水路","subcategoryTitleEn":"Dam monitoring, spillways and pressure waterways","learningTrack":"water","learningSubdiscipline":"water-hydraulics","learningTags":["water","water-hydraulics","water"],"architectureFamily":"water-hydraulic","architectureNodes":[["環形堰頂自由流","Circular crest free flow"],["豎井通水與空芯","Shaft water area and air core"],["旋渦環流與水頭","Swirl circulation and head"],["下游管流摩阻","Downstream conduit friction"],["瞬變量測與取樣","Transient measurement and sampling"]],"architectureEdges":[[0,1],[1,2],[2,3],[3,4],[0,3]],"diagram":{"type":"water-hydraulic","labels":["環形堰頂自由流","豎井通水與空芯","旋渦環流與水頭","下游管流摩阻","瞬變量測與取樣"],"labelsEn":["Circular crest free flow","Shaft water area and air core","Swirl circulation and head","Downstream conduit friction","Transient measurement and sampling"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"workedExample":{"title":"原創假想算例與邊界","titleEn":"Original hypothetical example and boundaries","text":"整合算例輸入全為教學假設，先檢查環形堰頂自由流：Assumed C=1.7 m0.5/s; crestDiameter=10 m; H=1 m; Q=1.7*pi*10*1**1.5=53.4071 m3/s；再獨立檢查喉部孔口控制：Cd=0.75; throatArea=12 m2; effectiveHead=8 m; Q=0.75*12*sqrt(2*9.81*8)=112.755 m3/s。敏感度：自由堰流近似下水頭由1增至1.5m，流量比為1.5的1.5次方即1.837；若轉為孔口控制且面積不變，同樣水頭比的流量比只有平方根1.225，因此需要確認控制轉換。 兩個結果須按各自量綱解釋，不能直接相加或當成完整設計。各算例分屬不同控制工況，不可把自由堰流與滿管流公式同時套在同一斷面。 將用同時入出流與水位量測核對庫容變化並檢查率定斜率作為獨立驗證，明確列出尚缺的現地輸入及其對結論的影響。","textEn":"Every input in this integrated example is a teaching assumption. First examine Circular crest free flow: Assumed C=1.7 m0.5/s; crestDiameter=10 m; H=1 m; Q=1.7*pi*10*1**1.5=53.4071 m3/s. Independently examine Throat orifice control: Cd=0.75; throatArea=12 m2; effectiveHead=8 m; Q=0.75*12*sqrt(2*9.81*8)=112.755 m3/s. Sensitivity: under free-weir control, increasing head from1 to1.5m gives a discharge ratio of1.837. Under fixed-area orifice control the same head ratio gives only1.225. A rating must therefore identify the change in control. Interpret each result in its own dimensions rather than adding them or treating them as a complete design. Examples represent different control regimes; free-weir and full-pipe relations must not be applied simultaneously at one section. Use the following independent check: Reconcile simultaneous inflow, outflow and stage change and inspect rating-curve slope. Identify missing field inputs and state which conclusions depend on them.","assumptions":"數值是本課自行設定的教學假設，不代表任何專案的設計值、量測值或規範允許值；改變系統邊界或荷載組合後必須重算。","assumptionsEn":"Inputs are teaching assumptions, not any project's design values, measurements or code allowances; recalculate after changing the system boundary or load combination.","sourceScope":"原創數值練習；來源支援公開原理與工程背景，不宣稱來源提供這組數據。","sourceScopeEn":"Original numerical exercise; sources support public principles and project context, not these numbers."},"depth":5,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"simulationOnly":true,"educationEdition":15,"enrichmentVersion":15,"stages":[{"id":"b248-v15-s1","title":"水文條件、邊界與工程系統","titleEn":"Hydrology, boundaries and engineering system","description":"本階段聚焦「環形堰頂自由流」與「喉部孔口控制」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Circular crest free flow\" and \"Throat orifice control\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b248-v15-01","title":"環形堰頂自由流：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Circular crest free flow: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-monticello","v15s-glen-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"objective":"說明「環形堰頂自由流」如何影響豎井式溢洪道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Circular crest free flow” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Shaft spillways”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"鐘口入口在低水頭下可近似環形堰流，周長提供有效堰長。接近流旋轉、墩柱與局部淹沒會降低均勻性；示意係數不能跨幾何直接沿用。水頭增加後控制可能移往喉部與隧道，應避免以同一冪次延伸整條率定曲線。 驗證時應沿環形堰頂量測水頭並觀察各方位水舌是否對稱，並辨識以下失效情境：偏心接近流會形成非均勻溢流並改變率定。這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「環形堰頂自由流」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"At low head a bellmouth can behave approximately as a circular weir, with circumference supplying crest length. Swirl, piers and submergence reduce uniformity. An illustrative coefficient cannot transfer across geometries, and higher heads may move control to the throat or tunnel rather than preserve one power law. Test this interpretation with the following evidence: Measure head around the circular crest and observe whether nappes are symmetric. In particular, distinguish this failure mechanism: Eccentric approach flow creates nonuniform overflow and changes the rating. That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Circular crest free flow” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：Assumed C=1.7 m0.5/s; crestDiameter=10 m; H=1 m; Q=1.7*pi*10*1**1.5=53.4071 m3/s。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: Assumed C=1.7 m0.5/s; crestDiameter=10 m; H=1 m; Q=1.7*pi*10*1**1.5=53.4071 m3/s.","failure":"常見誤解：「環形堰率定可以延伸到任何高水頭工況」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A circular-weir rating remains valid at every high-head condition\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「環形堰頂自由流」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Circular crest free flow”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b248-v15-01-k1","title":"環形堰頂自由流","titleEn":"Circular crest free flow","text":"鐘口入口在低水頭下可近似環形堰流，周長提供有效堰長。接近流旋轉、墩柱與局部淹沒會降低均勻性；示意係數不能跨幾何直接沿用。","textEn":"At low head a bellmouth can behave approximately as a circular weir, with circumference supplying crest length. Swirl, piers and submergence reduce uniformity.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-monticello","v15s-glen-owner"]},{"id":"b248-v15-01-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：環形堰率定可以延伸到任何高水頭工況 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A circular-weir rating remains valid at every high-head condition Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-monticello","v15s-glen-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「環形堰頂自由流」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Circular crest free flow\" is correct?","options":["環形堰率定可以延伸到任何高水頭工況","鐘口入口在低水頭下可近似環形堰流，周長提供有效堰長。","孔口控制的流量仍必定與水頭一點五次方成正比"],"optionsEn":["A circular-weir rating remains valid at every high-head condition","At low head a bellmouth can behave approximately as a circular weir, with circumference supplying crest length.","Orifice discharge must remain proportional to head to the three-halves power"],"answer":1,"explanation":"鐘口入口在低水頭下可近似環形堰流，周長提供有效堰長。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"At low head a bellmouth can behave approximately as a circular weir, with circumference supplying crest length. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":1},{"id":"b248-v15-02","title":"環形堰頂自由流：定量估算","titleEn":"Circular crest free flow: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-monticello","v15s-glen-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b248-v15-01"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「環形堰頂自由流」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Circular crest free flow” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：Assumed C=1.7 m0.5/s; crestDiameter=10 m; H=1 m; Q=1.7*pi*10*1**1.5=53.4071 m3/s。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: Assumed C=1.7 m0.5/s; crestDiameter=10 m; H=1 m; Q=1.7*pi*10*1**1.5=53.4071 m3/s. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：沿環形堰頂量測水頭並觀察各方位水舌是否對稱。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Measure head around the circular crest and observe whether nappes are symmetric.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b248-v15-02-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：Assumed C=1.7 m0.5/s; crestDiameter=10 m; H=1 m; Q=1.7*pi*10*1**1.5=53.4071 m3/s。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: Assumed C=1.7 m0.5/s; crestDiameter=10 m; H=1 m; Q=1.7*pi*10*1**1.5=53.4071 m3/s. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-monticello","v15s-glen-owner"]},{"id":"b248-v15-02-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-monticello","v15s-glen-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「環形堰頂自由流」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Circular crest free flow\", which statement holds?","options":["通氣管存在就保證任何流量下都能充分補氣","動量變化單項就是井底彎道全部荷載","原創教學假設：Assumed C=1.7 m0.5/s; crestDiameter=10 m; H=1 m; Q=1.7*pi*10*1**1.5=53.4071 m3/s。"],"optionsEn":["A vent pipe guarantees adequate air supply at every water discharge","Momentum change alone equals the entire bottom-bend load","Original teaching assumptions: Assumed C=1.7 m0.5/s; crestDiameter=10 m; H=1 m; Q=1.7*pi*10*1**1.5=53.4071 m3/s."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設：Assumed C=1.7 m0.5/s; crestDiameter=10 m; H=1 m; Q=1.7*pi*10*1**1.5=53.4071 m3/s。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: Assumed C=1.7 m0.5/s; crestDiameter=10 m; H=1 m; Q=1.7*pi*10*1**1.5=53.4071 m3/s. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":2},{"id":"b248-v15-03","title":"環形堰頂自由流：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Circular crest free flow: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-monticello","v15s-glen-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b248-v15-02"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「環形堰頂自由流」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Circular crest free flow” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"沿環形堰頂量測水頭並觀察各方位水舌是否對稱。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「偏心接近流會形成非均勻溢流並改變率定」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Measure head around the circular crest and observe whether nappes are symmetric. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: Eccentric approach flow creates nonuniform overflow and changes the rating. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：交接時以沿環形堰頂量測水頭並觀察各方位水舌是否對稱作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對偏心接近流會形成非均勻溢流並改變率定，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","observationEn":"Site practice: At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Measure head around the circular crest and observe whether nappes are symmetric. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: Eccentric approach flow creates nonuniform overflow and changes the rating. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","failure":"注意干擾：偏心接近流會形成非均勻溢流並改變率定。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Eccentric approach flow creates nonuniform overflow and changes the rating. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b248-v15-03-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"沿環形堰頂量測水頭並觀察各方位水舌是否對稱。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「偏心接近流會形成非均勻溢流並改變率定」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。","textEn":"Measure head around the circular crest and observe whether nappes are symmetric. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: Eccentric approach flow creates nonuniform overflow and changes the rating. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-monticello","v15s-glen-owner"]},{"id":"b248-v15-03-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"交接時以沿環形堰頂量測水頭並觀察各方位水舌是否對稱作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對偏心接近流會形成非均勻溢流並改變率定，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","textEn":"At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Measure head around the circular crest and observe whether nappes are symmetric. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: Eccentric approach flow creates nonuniform overflow and changes the rating. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-monticello","v15s-glen-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「環形堰頂自由流」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Circular crest free flow\"?","options":["沿環形堰頂量測水頭並觀察各方位水舌是否對稱。","量測時不必記錄溫度、水頭、水位歷程與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","靜態單點洩量足以完成任何洪水演算"],"optionsEn":["Measure head around the circular crest and observe whether nappes are symmetric.","Temperature, water head, water-level history and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","One static discharge point is sufficient to route every flood"],"answer":0,"explanation":"沿環形堰頂量測水頭並觀察各方位水舌是否對稱。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Measure head around the circular crest and observe whether nappes are symmetric. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":3},{"id":"b248-v15-04","title":"環形堰頂自由流：失效診斷","titleEn":"Circular crest free flow: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-monticello","v15s-glen-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b248-v15-03"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「環形堰頂自由流」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Circular crest free flow” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"偏心接近流會形成非均勻溢流並改變率定。診斷時應採取以下查核：沿環形堰頂量測水頭並觀察各方位水舌是否對稱，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Eccentric approach flow creates nonuniform overflow and changes the rating. Diagnose it by the following check: Measure head around the circular crest and observe whether nappes are symmetric. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「環形堰率定可以延伸到任何高水頭工況」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A circular-weir rating remains valid at every high-head condition\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b248-v15-04-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"偏心接近流會形成非均勻溢流並改變率定。診斷時應採取以下查核：沿環形堰頂量測水頭並觀察各方位水舌是否對稱，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。","textEn":"Eccentric approach flow creates nonuniform overflow and changes the rating. Diagnose it by the following check: Measure head around the circular crest and observe whether nappes are symmetric. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-monticello","v15s-glen-owner"]},{"id":"b248-v15-04-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-monticello","v15s-glen-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「環形堰頂自由流」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Circular crest free flow\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","偏心接近流會形成非均勻溢流並改變率定。","孔口控制的流量仍必定與水頭一點五次方成正比"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Eccentric approach flow creates nonuniform overflow and changes the rating.","Orifice discharge must remain proportional to head to the three-halves power"],"answer":1,"explanation":"偏心接近流會形成非均勻溢流並改變率定。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Eccentric approach flow creates nonuniform overflow and changes the rating. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":4},{"id":"b248-v15-05","title":"喉部孔口控制：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Throat orifice control: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-monticello","v15s-glen-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b248-v15-04"],"objective":"說明「喉部孔口控制」如何影響豎井式溢洪道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Throat orifice control” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Shaft spillways”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"喉部淹沒後可能由有效孔口面積與水頭差控制流量，流量對水頭的反應比自由堰流緩。排氣、下游壓力與流量係數都會影響此關係；孔口公式並不描述控制轉換期間的劇烈波動，需以連續升降流量試驗辨認。 驗證時應在升流與降流過程比較喉部壓力和水位流量曲線，並辨識以下失效情境：控制轉換滯回可能使同水位出現不同流量。這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「喉部孔口控制」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Once submerged, the throat may act as an orifice governed by effective area and head difference. Discharge then responds less strongly to head than free-weir flow. Venting, downstream pressure and coefficient matter, and the equation does not describe unstable transitions between these regimes. Test this interpretation with the following evidence: Compare throat pressure and stage-discharge curves during increasing and decreasing flow. In particular, distinguish this failure mechanism: Transition hysteresis may produce different discharges at the same stage. That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Throat orifice control” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：Cd=0.75; throatArea=12 m2; effectiveHead=8 m; Q=0.75*12*sqrt(2*9.81*8)=112.755 m3/s。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: Cd=0.75; throatArea=12 m2; effectiveHead=8 m; Q=0.75*12*sqrt(2*9.81*8)=112.755 m3/s.","failure":"常見誤解：「孔口控制的流量仍必定與水頭一點五次方成正比」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Orifice discharge must remain proportional to head to the three-halves power\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「喉部孔口控制」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Throat orifice control”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b248-v15-05-k1","title":"喉部孔口控制","titleEn":"Throat orifice control","text":"喉部淹沒後可能由有效孔口面積與水頭差控制流量，流量對水頭的反應比自由堰流緩。排氣、下游壓力與流量係數都會影響此關係；孔口公式並不描述控制轉換期間的劇烈波動，需以連續升降流量試驗辨認。","textEn":"Once submerged, the throat may act as an orifice governed by effective area and head difference. Discharge then responds less strongly to head than free-weir flow.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-monticello","v15s-glen-owner"]},{"id":"b248-v15-05-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：孔口控制的流量仍必定與水頭一點五次方成正比 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Orifice discharge must remain proportional to head to the three-halves power Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-monticello","v15s-glen-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「喉部孔口控制」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Throat orifice control\" is correct?","options":["孔口控制的流量仍必定與水頭一點五次方成正比","整個豎井截面在所有工況都充滿液態水","喉部淹沒後可能由有效孔口面積與水頭差控制流量，流量對水頭的反應比自由堰流緩。"],"optionsEn":["Orifice discharge must remain proportional to head to the three-halves power","The entire shaft section contains liquid water in every operating regime","Once submerged, the throat may act as an orifice governed by effective area and head difference."],"answer":2,"explanation":"喉部淹沒後可能由有效孔口面積與水頭差控制流量，流量對水頭的反應比自由堰流緩。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Once submerged, the throat may act as an orifice governed by effective area and head difference. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":5},{"id":"b248-v15-06","title":"喉部孔口控制：定量估算","titleEn":"Throat orifice control: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-monticello","v15s-glen-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b248-v15-05"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「喉部孔口控制」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Throat orifice control” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：Cd=0.75; throatArea=12 m2; effectiveHead=8 m; Q=0.75*12*sqrt(2*9.81*8)=112.755 m3/s。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: Cd=0.75; throatArea=12 m2; effectiveHead=8 m; Q=0.75*12*sqrt(2*9.81*8)=112.755 m3/s. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：在升流與降流過程比較喉部壓力和水位流量曲線。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Compare throat pressure and stage-discharge curves during increasing and decreasing flow.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b248-v15-06-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：Cd=0.75; throatArea=12 m2; effectiveHead=8 m; Q=0.75*12*sqrt(2*9.81*8)=112.755 m3/s。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: Cd=0.75; throatArea=12 m2; effectiveHead=8 m; Q=0.75*12*sqrt(2*9.81*8)=112.755 m3/s. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-monticello","v15s-glen-owner"]},{"id":"b248-v15-06-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-monticello","v15s-glen-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「喉部孔口控制」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Throat orifice control\", which statement holds?","options":["原創教學假設：Cd=0.75; throatArea=12 m2; effectiveHead=8 m; Q=0.75*12*sqrt(2*9.81*8)=112.755 m3/s。","平均入流速度低就不可能形成進水旋渦","下游管徑夠大就可以忽略全部摩阻"],"optionsEn":["Original teaching assumptions: Cd=0.75; throatArea=12 m2; effectiveHead=8 m; Q=0.75*12*sqrt(2*9.81*8)=112.755 m3/s.","Low mean approach speed makes inlet vortices impossible","A sufficiently large downstream pipe permits ignoring all friction losses"],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創教學假設：Cd=0.75; throatArea=12 m2; effectiveHead=8 m; Q=0.75*12*sqrt(2*9.81*8)=112.755 m3/s。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: Cd=0.75; throatArea=12 m2; effectiveHead=8 m; Q=0.75*12*sqrt(2*9.81*8)=112.755 m3/s. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":6},{"id":"b248-v15-07","title":"喉部孔口控制：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Throat orifice control: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-monticello","v15s-glen-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b248-v15-06"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「喉部孔口控制」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Throat orifice control” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"在升流與降流過程比較喉部壓力和水位流量曲線。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「控制轉換滯回可能使同水位出現不同流量」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Compare throat pressure and stage-discharge curves during increasing and decreasing flow. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: Transition hysteresis may produce different discharges at the same stage. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：交接時以在升流與降流過程比較喉部壓力和水位流量曲線作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對控制轉換滯回可能使同水位出現不同流量，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","observationEn":"Site practice: At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Compare throat pressure and stage-discharge curves during increasing and decreasing flow. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: Transition hysteresis may produce different discharges at the same stage. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","failure":"注意干擾：控制轉換滯回可能使同水位出現不同流量。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Transition hysteresis may produce different discharges at the same stage. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b248-v15-07-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"在升流與降流過程比較喉部壓力和水位流量曲線。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「控制轉換滯回可能使同水位出現不同流量」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。","textEn":"Compare throat pressure and stage-discharge curves during increasing and decreasing flow. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: Transition hysteresis may produce different discharges at the same stage. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-monticello","v15s-glen-owner"]},{"id":"b248-v15-07-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"交接時以在升流與降流過程比較喉部壓力和水位流量曲線作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對控制轉換滯回可能使同水位出現不同流量，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","textEn":"At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Compare throat pressure and stage-discharge curves during increasing and decreasing flow. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: Transition hysteresis may produce different discharges at the same stage. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-monticello","v15s-glen-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「喉部孔口控制」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Throat orifice control\"?","options":["沿用另一處水工設施或流域的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","在升流與降流過程比較喉部壓力和水位流量曲線。","堵塞面積減少三成就保證洩量只減三成"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another hydraulic structure or catchment counts as verifying this structure.","Compare throat pressure and stage-discharge curves during increasing and decreasing flow.","A thirty-percent area blockage guarantees exactly thirty-percent discharge loss"],"answer":1,"explanation":"在升流與降流過程比較喉部壓力和水位流量曲線。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Compare throat pressure and stage-discharge curves during increasing and decreasing flow. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":7},{"id":"b248-v15-08","title":"喉部孔口控制：失效診斷","titleEn":"Throat orifice control: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-monticello","v15s-glen-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b248-v15-07"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「喉部孔口控制」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Throat orifice control” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"控制轉換滯回可能使同水位出現不同流量。診斷時應採取以下查核：在升流與降流過程比較喉部壓力和水位流量曲線，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Transition hysteresis may produce different discharges at the same stage. Diagnose it by the following check: Compare throat pressure and stage-discharge curves during increasing and decreasing flow. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「孔口控制的流量仍必定與水頭一點五次方成正比」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Orifice discharge must remain proportional to head to the three-halves power\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b248-v15-08-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"控制轉換滯回可能使同水位出現不同流量。診斷時應採取以下查核：在升流與降流過程比較喉部壓力和水位流量曲線，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。","textEn":"Transition hysteresis may produce different discharges at the same stage. Diagnose it by the following check: Compare throat pressure and stage-discharge curves during increasing and decreasing flow. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-monticello","v15s-glen-owner"]},{"id":"b248-v15-08-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-monticello","v15s-glen-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「喉部孔口控制」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Throat orifice control\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","整個豎井截面在所有工況都充滿液態水","控制轉換滯回可能使同水位出現不同流量。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","The entire shaft section contains liquid water in every operating regime","Transition hysteresis may produce different discharges at the same stage."],"answer":2,"explanation":"控制轉換滯回可能使同水位出現不同流量。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Transition hysteresis may produce different discharges at the same stage. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":8}],"order":1},{"id":"b248-v15-s2","title":"水力機制、材料與定量模型","titleEn":"Hydraulics, materials and quantitative models","description":"本階段聚焦「豎井通水與空芯」與「通氣需求與管徑」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Shaft water area and air core\" and \"Vent demand and duct area\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b248-v15-09","title":"豎井通水與空芯：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Shaft water area and air core: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-monticello","v15s-glen-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b248-v15-08"],"objective":"說明「豎井通水與空芯」如何影響豎井式溢洪道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Shaft water area and air core” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Shaft spillways”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"豎井中沿壁水膜與中央空氣芯可能並存，水量連續應只用液相過水面積。簡化環狀截面忽略含氣與非均勻流速，仍可提醒學生不能將整個井徑都算成水流面積；空芯縮小也會改變通氣和壓力邊界。 驗證時應以影像或含氣探針確認空芯尺寸並核對液相流量，並辨識以下失效情境：空芯收縮可能使原本開放通氣轉成受限流動。這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「豎井通水與空芯」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"A wall-attached water layer can surround an air core. Liquid continuity therefore uses the water area rather than the full shaft. A simple annulus omits aeration and velocity variation but shows why air-core changes affect both mean liquid speed and the ventilation boundary. Test this interpretation with the following evidence: Use imaging or air probes to establish air-core size and check liquid discharge. In particular, distinguish this failure mechanism: Air-core contraction can turn open ventilation into restricted flow. That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Shaft water area and air core” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：shaftDiameter=5 m; airCoreDiameter=3 m; liquidArea=pi*(5**2-3**2)/4=12.5664 m2。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: shaftDiameter=5 m; airCoreDiameter=3 m; liquidArea=pi*(5**2-3**2)/4=12.5664 m2.","failure":"常見誤解：「整個豎井截面在所有工況都充滿液態水」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"The entire shaft section contains liquid water in every operating regime\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「豎井通水與空芯」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Shaft water area and air core”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b248-v15-09-k1","title":"豎井通水與空芯","titleEn":"Shaft water area and air core","text":"豎井中沿壁水膜與中央空氣芯可能並存，水量連續應只用液相過水面積。簡化環狀截面忽略含氣與非均勻流速，仍可提醒學生不能將整個井徑都算成水流面積；空芯縮小也會改變通氣和壓力邊界。","textEn":"A wall-attached water layer can surround an air core. Liquid continuity therefore uses the water area rather than the full shaft.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-monticello","v15s-glen-owner"]},{"id":"b248-v15-09-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：整個豎井截面在所有工況都充滿液態水 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: The entire shaft section contains liquid water in every operating regime Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-monticello","v15s-glen-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「豎井通水與空芯」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Shaft water area and air core\" is correct?","options":["豎井中沿壁水膜與中央空氣芯可能並存，水量連續應只用液相過水面積。","整個豎井截面在所有工況都充滿液態水","通氣管存在就保證任何流量下都能充分補氣"],"optionsEn":["A wall-attached water layer can surround an air core.","The entire shaft section contains liquid water in every operating regime","A vent pipe guarantees adequate air supply at every water discharge"],"answer":0,"explanation":"豎井中沿壁水膜與中央空氣芯可能並存，水量連續應只用液相過水面積。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"A wall-attached water layer can surround an air core. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":9},{"id":"b248-v15-10","title":"豎井通水與空芯：定量估算","titleEn":"Shaft water area and air core: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-monticello","v15s-glen-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b248-v15-09"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「豎井通水與空芯」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Shaft water area and air core” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：shaftDiameter=5 m; airCoreDiameter=3 m; liquidArea=pi*(5**2-3**2)/4=12.5664 m2。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: shaftDiameter=5 m; airCoreDiameter=3 m; liquidArea=pi*(5**2-3**2)/4=12.5664 m2. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以影像或含氣探針確認空芯尺寸並核對液相流量。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Use imaging or air probes to establish air-core size and check liquid discharge.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b248-v15-10-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：shaftDiameter=5 m; airCoreDiameter=3 m; liquidArea=pi*(5**2-3**2)/4=12.5664 m2。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: shaftDiameter=5 m; airCoreDiameter=3 m; liquidArea=pi*(5**2-3**2)/4=12.5664 m2. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-monticello","v15s-glen-owner"]},{"id":"b248-v15-10-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-monticello","v15s-glen-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「豎井通水與空芯」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Shaft water area and air core\", which statement holds?","options":["動量變化單項就是井底彎道全部荷載","原創教學假設：shaftDiameter=5 m; airCoreDiameter=3 m; liquidArea=pi*(5**2-3**2)/4=12.5664 m2。","靜態單點洩量足以完成任何洪水演算"],"optionsEn":["Momentum change alone equals the entire bottom-bend load","Original teaching assumptions: shaftDiameter=5 m; airCoreDiameter=3 m; liquidArea=pi*(5**2-3**2)/4=12.5664 m2.","One static discharge point is sufficient to route every flood"],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創教學假設：shaftDiameter=5 m; airCoreDiameter=3 m; liquidArea=pi*(5**2-3**2)/4=12.5664 m2。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: shaftDiameter=5 m; airCoreDiameter=3 m; liquidArea=pi*(5**2-3**2)/4=12.5664 m2. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":10},{"id":"b248-v15-11","title":"豎井通水與空芯：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Shaft water area and air core: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-monticello","v15s-glen-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b248-v15-10"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「豎井通水與空芯」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Shaft water area and air core” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以影像或含氣探針確認空芯尺寸並核對液相流量。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「空芯收縮可能使原本開放通氣轉成受限流動」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Use imaging or air probes to establish air-core size and check liquid discharge. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: Air-core contraction can turn open ventilation into restricted flow. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：交接時以以影像或含氣探針確認空芯尺寸並核對液相流量作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對空芯收縮可能使原本開放通氣轉成受限流動，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","observationEn":"Site practice: At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Use imaging or air probes to establish air-core size and check liquid discharge. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: Air-core contraction can turn open ventilation into restricted flow. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","failure":"注意干擾：空芯收縮可能使原本開放通氣轉成受限流動。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Air-core contraction can turn open ventilation into restricted flow. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b248-v15-11-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以影像或含氣探針確認空芯尺寸並核對液相流量。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「空芯收縮可能使原本開放通氣轉成受限流動」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。","textEn":"Use imaging or air probes to establish air-core size and check liquid discharge. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: Air-core contraction can turn open ventilation into restricted flow. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-monticello","v15s-glen-owner"]},{"id":"b248-v15-11-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"交接時以以影像或含氣探針確認空芯尺寸並核對液相流量作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對空芯收縮可能使原本開放通氣轉成受限流動，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","textEn":"At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Use imaging or air probes to establish air-core size and check liquid discharge. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: Air-core contraction can turn open ventilation into restricted flow. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-monticello","v15s-glen-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「豎井通水與空芯」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Shaft water area and air core\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","只達兩倍頻率就保證所有壓力尖峰量測準確","以影像或含氣探針確認空芯尺寸並核對液相流量。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","Sampling at twice the frequency guarantees accurate measurement of every pressure peak","Use imaging or air probes to establish air-core size and check liquid discharge."],"answer":2,"explanation":"以影像或含氣探針確認空芯尺寸並核對液相流量。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Use imaging or air probes to establish air-core size and check liquid discharge. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":11},{"id":"b248-v15-12","title":"豎井通水與空芯：失效診斷","titleEn":"Shaft water area and air core: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-monticello","v15s-glen-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b248-v15-11"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「豎井通水與空芯」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Shaft water area and air core” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"空芯收縮可能使原本開放通氣轉成受限流動。診斷時應採取以下查核：以影像或含氣探針確認空芯尺寸並核對液相流量，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Air-core contraction can turn open ventilation into restricted flow. Diagnose it by the following check: Use imaging or air probes to establish air-core size and check liquid discharge. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「整個豎井截面在所有工況都充滿液態水」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"The entire shaft section contains liquid water in every operating regime\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b248-v15-12-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"空芯收縮可能使原本開放通氣轉成受限流動。診斷時應採取以下查核：以影像或含氣探針確認空芯尺寸並核對液相流量，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。","textEn":"Air-core contraction can turn open ventilation into restricted flow. Diagnose it by the following check: Use imaging or air probes to establish air-core size and check liquid discharge. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-monticello","v15s-glen-owner"]},{"id":"b248-v15-12-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-monticello","v15s-glen-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「豎井通水與空芯」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Shaft water area and air core\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["空芯收縮可能使原本開放通氣轉成受限流動。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","通氣管存在就保證任何流量下都能充分補氣"],"optionsEn":["Air-core contraction can turn open ventilation into restricted flow.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","A vent pipe guarantees adequate air supply at every water discharge"],"answer":0,"explanation":"空芯收縮可能使原本開放通氣轉成受限流動。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Air-core contraction can turn open ventilation into restricted flow. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":12},{"id":"b248-v15-13","title":"通氣需求與管徑：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Vent demand and duct area: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-monticello","v15s-glen-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b248-v15-12"],"objective":"說明「通氣需求與管徑」如何影響豎井式溢洪道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Vent demand and duct area” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Shaft spillways”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"水流捲帶空氣進入下游通道，補氣不足會造成低壓與不穩定振盪。給定空氣體積流量與允許平均速度可作截面盤點，不能代替可壓縮流與入口損失分析；空氣體積需標明當地壓力溫度，否則密度與流量不可比。 驗證時應同步記錄通氣管空氣流量與井內絕對壓力，並辨識以下失效情境：鳥網或雜物堵塞會增加通氣阻力並放大負壓。這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「通氣需求與管徑」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Entrained air must be replaced through ventilation paths; insufficient supply can cause low pressure and oscillation. Area from specified air volume and speed is only a continuity check, not compressible-flow or inlet-loss analysis. State local pressure and temperature when reporting air volume to preserve comparability. Test this interpretation with the following evidence: Record vent airflow and shaft absolute pressure simultaneously. In particular, distinguish this failure mechanism: Screens or debris blockage increases ventilation resistance and deepens subpressure. That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Vent demand and duct area” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：AirVolumeAtLocalConditions=15 m3/s; meanAirVelocity=12 m/s; requiredFlowArea=15/12=1.25 m2。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: AirVolumeAtLocalConditions=15 m3/s; meanAirVelocity=12 m/s; requiredFlowArea=15/12=1.25 m2.","failure":"常見誤解：「通氣管存在就保證任何流量下都能充分補氣」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A vent pipe guarantees adequate air supply at every water discharge\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「通氣需求與管徑」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Vent demand and duct area”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b248-v15-13-k1","title":"通氣需求與管徑","titleEn":"Vent demand and duct area","text":"水流捲帶空氣進入下游通道，補氣不足會造成低壓與不穩定振盪。給定空氣體積流量與允許平均速度可作截面盤點，不能代替可壓縮流與入口損失分析；空氣體積需標明當地壓力溫度，否則密度與流量不可比。","textEn":"Entrained air must be replaced through ventilation paths; insufficient supply can cause low pressure and oscillation. Area from specified air volume and speed is only a continuity check, not compressible-flow or inlet-loss analysis.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-monticello","v15s-glen-owner"]},{"id":"b248-v15-13-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：通氣管存在就保證任何流量下都能充分補氣 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A vent pipe guarantees adequate air supply at every water discharge Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-monticello","v15s-glen-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「通氣需求與管徑」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Vent demand and duct area\" is correct?","options":["通氣管存在就保證任何流量下都能充分補氣","水流捲帶空氣進入下游通道，補氣不足會造成低壓與不穩定振盪。","平均入流速度低就不可能形成進水旋渦"],"optionsEn":["A vent pipe guarantees adequate air supply at every water discharge","Entrained air must be replaced through ventilation paths; insufficient supply can cause low pressure and oscillation.","Low mean approach speed makes inlet vortices impossible"],"answer":1,"explanation":"水流捲帶空氣進入下游通道，補氣不足會造成低壓與不穩定振盪。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Entrained air must be replaced through ventilation paths; insufficient supply can cause low pressure and oscillation. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":13},{"id":"b248-v15-14","title":"通氣需求與管徑：定量估算","titleEn":"Vent demand and duct area: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-monticello","v15s-glen-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b248-v15-13"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「通氣需求與管徑」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Vent demand and duct area” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：AirVolumeAtLocalConditions=15 m3/s; meanAirVelocity=12 m/s; requiredFlowArea=15/12=1.25 m2。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: AirVolumeAtLocalConditions=15 m3/s; meanAirVelocity=12 m/s; requiredFlowArea=15/12=1.25 m2. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：同步記錄通氣管空氣流量與井內絕對壓力。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Record vent airflow and shaft absolute pressure simultaneously.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b248-v15-14-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：AirVolumeAtLocalConditions=15 m3/s; meanAirVelocity=12 m/s; requiredFlowArea=15/12=1.25 m2。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: AirVolumeAtLocalConditions=15 m3/s; meanAirVelocity=12 m/s; requiredFlowArea=15/12=1.25 m2. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-monticello","v15s-glen-owner"]},{"id":"b248-v15-14-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-monticello","v15s-glen-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「通氣需求與管徑」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Vent demand and duct area\", which statement holds?","options":["下游管徑夠大就可以忽略全部摩阻","堵塞面積減少三成就保證洩量只減三成","原創教學假設：AirVolumeAtLocalConditions=15 m3/s; meanAirVelocity=12 m/s; requiredFlowArea=15/12=1.25 m2。"],"optionsEn":["A sufficiently large downstream pipe permits ignoring all friction losses","A thirty-percent area blockage guarantees exactly thirty-percent discharge loss","Original teaching assumptions: AirVolumeAtLocalConditions=15 m3/s; meanAirVelocity=12 m/s; requiredFlowArea=15/12=1.25 m2."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設：AirVolumeAtLocalConditions=15 m3/s; meanAirVelocity=12 m/s; requiredFlowArea=15/12=1.25 m2。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: AirVolumeAtLocalConditions=15 m3/s; meanAirVelocity=12 m/s; requiredFlowArea=15/12=1.25 m2. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":14},{"id":"b248-v15-15","title":"通氣需求與管徑：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Vent demand and duct area: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-monticello","v15s-glen-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b248-v15-14"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「通氣需求與管徑」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Vent demand and duct area” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"同步記錄通氣管空氣流量與井內絕對壓力。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「鳥網或雜物堵塞會增加通氣阻力並放大負壓」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Record vent airflow and shaft absolute pressure simultaneously. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: Screens or debris blockage increases ventilation resistance and deepens subpressure. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：交接時以同步記錄通氣管空氣流量與井內絕對壓力作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對鳥網或雜物堵塞會增加通氣阻力並放大負壓，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","observationEn":"Site practice: At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Record vent airflow and shaft absolute pressure simultaneously. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: Screens or debris blockage increases ventilation resistance and deepens subpressure. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","failure":"注意干擾：鳥網或雜物堵塞會增加通氣阻力並放大負壓。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Screens or debris blockage increases ventilation resistance and deepens subpressure. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b248-v15-15-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"同步記錄通氣管空氣流量與井內絕對壓力。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「鳥網或雜物堵塞會增加通氣阻力並放大負壓」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。","textEn":"Record vent airflow and shaft absolute pressure simultaneously. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: Screens or debris blockage increases ventilation resistance and deepens subpressure. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-monticello","v15s-glen-owner"]},{"id":"b248-v15-15-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"交接時以同步記錄通氣管空氣流量與井內絕對壓力作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對鳥網或雜物堵塞會增加通氣阻力並放大負壓，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","textEn":"At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Record vent airflow and shaft absolute pressure simultaneously. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: Screens or debris blockage increases ventilation resistance and deepens subpressure. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-monticello","v15s-glen-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「通氣需求與管徑」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Vent demand and duct area\"?","options":["同步記錄通氣管空氣流量與井內絕對壓力。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","環形堰率定可以延伸到任何高水頭工況"],"optionsEn":["Record vent airflow and shaft absolute pressure simultaneously.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","A circular-weir rating remains valid at every high-head condition"],"answer":0,"explanation":"同步記錄通氣管空氣流量與井內絕對壓力。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Record vent airflow and shaft absolute pressure simultaneously. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":15},{"id":"b248-v15-16","title":"通氣需求與管徑：失效診斷","titleEn":"Vent demand and duct area: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-monticello","v15s-glen-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b248-v15-15"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「通氣需求與管徑」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Vent demand and duct area” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"鳥網或雜物堵塞會增加通氣阻力並放大負壓。診斷時應採取以下查核：同步記錄通氣管空氣流量與井內絕對壓力，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Screens or debris blockage increases ventilation resistance and deepens subpressure. Diagnose it by the following check: Record vent airflow and shaft absolute pressure simultaneously. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「通氣管存在就保證任何流量下都能充分補氣」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A vent pipe guarantees adequate air supply at every water discharge\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b248-v15-16-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"鳥網或雜物堵塞會增加通氣阻力並放大負壓。診斷時應採取以下查核：同步記錄通氣管空氣流量與井內絕對壓力，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。","textEn":"Screens or debris blockage increases ventilation resistance and deepens subpressure. Diagnose it by the following check: Record vent airflow and shaft absolute pressure simultaneously. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-monticello","v15s-glen-owner"]},{"id":"b248-v15-16-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-monticello","v15s-glen-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「通氣需求與管徑」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Vent demand and duct area\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","鳥網或雜物堵塞會增加通氣阻力並放大負壓。","平均入流速度低就不可能形成進水旋渦"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Screens or debris blockage increases ventilation resistance and deepens subpressure.","Low mean approach speed makes inlet vortices impossible"],"answer":1,"explanation":"鳥網或雜物堵塞會增加通氣阻力並放大負壓。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Screens or debris blockage increases ventilation resistance and deepens subpressure. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":16}],"order":2},{"id":"b248-v15-s3","title":"施工方法與施工階段控制","titleEn":"Construction methods and stage control","description":"本階段聚焦「旋渦環流與水頭」與「豎井底彎轉動量」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Swirl circulation and head\" and \"Bottom bend momentum change\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b248-v15-17","title":"旋渦環流與水頭：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Swirl circulation and head: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-monticello","v15s-glen-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b248-v15-16"],"objective":"說明「旋渦環流與水頭」如何影響豎井式溢洪道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Swirl circulation and head” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Shaft spillways”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"不對稱接近流可能產生環流與空氣渦，局部旋轉速度會降低中心壓力並影響進流容量。自由渦近似僅在指定半徑之外有效，靠近渦核不能任意外推至無限速度；抗渦構件應以模型驗證其阻水與導流作用。 驗證時應以表面追蹤與速度量測辨識環流方向和渦核範圍，並辨識以下失效情境：只降低平均入流速度可能仍保留強烈環流。這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「旋渦環流與水頭」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Asymmetric approach flow can create circulation and an air-core vortex. Tangential velocity affects central pressure and inlet capacity. A free-vortex model applies only outside a specified core and cannot be extrapolated to infinite center velocity; test antivortex devices for both flow guidance and obstruction. Test this interpretation with the following evidence: Track the surface and measure velocities to identify circulation and core extent. In particular, distinguish this failure mechanism: Reducing mean approach speed alone may leave strong circulation. That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Swirl circulation and head” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：Circulation=20 m2/s; radius=2 m; tangentialV=20/(2*pi*2)=1.59155 m/s。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: Circulation=20 m2/s; radius=2 m; tangentialV=20/(2*pi*2)=1.59155 m/s.","failure":"常見誤解：「平均入流速度低就不可能形成進水旋渦」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Low mean approach speed makes inlet vortices impossible\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「旋渦環流與水頭」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Swirl circulation and head”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b248-v15-17-k1","title":"旋渦環流與水頭","titleEn":"Swirl circulation and head","text":"不對稱接近流可能產生環流與空氣渦，局部旋轉速度會降低中心壓力並影響進流容量。自由渦近似僅在指定半徑之外有效，靠近渦核不能任意外推至無限速度；抗渦構件應以模型驗證其阻水與導流作用。","textEn":"Asymmetric approach flow can create circulation and an air-core vortex. Tangential velocity affects central pressure and inlet capacity.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-monticello","v15s-glen-owner"]},{"id":"b248-v15-17-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：平均入流速度低就不可能形成進水旋渦 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Low mean approach speed makes inlet vortices impossible Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-monticello","v15s-glen-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「旋渦環流與水頭」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Swirl circulation and head\" is correct?","options":["平均入流速度低就不可能形成進水旋渦","動量變化單項就是井底彎道全部荷載","不對稱接近流可能產生環流與空氣渦，局部旋轉速度會降低中心壓力並影響進流容量。"],"optionsEn":["Low mean approach speed makes inlet vortices impossible","Momentum change alone equals the entire bottom-bend load","Asymmetric approach flow can create circulation and an air-core vortex."],"answer":2,"explanation":"不對稱接近流可能產生環流與空氣渦，局部旋轉速度會降低中心壓力並影響進流容量。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Asymmetric approach flow can create circulation and an air-core vortex. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":17},{"id":"b248-v15-18","title":"旋渦環流與水頭：定量估算","titleEn":"Swirl circulation and head: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-monticello","v15s-glen-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b248-v15-17"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「旋渦環流與水頭」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Swirl circulation and head” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：Circulation=20 m2/s; radius=2 m; tangentialV=20/(2*pi*2)=1.59155 m/s。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: Circulation=20 m2/s; radius=2 m; tangentialV=20/(2*pi*2)=1.59155 m/s. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以表面追蹤與速度量測辨識環流方向和渦核範圍。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Track the surface and measure velocities to identify circulation and core extent.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b248-v15-18-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：Circulation=20 m2/s; radius=2 m; tangentialV=20/(2*pi*2)=1.59155 m/s。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: Circulation=20 m2/s; radius=2 m; tangentialV=20/(2*pi*2)=1.59155 m/s. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-monticello","v15s-glen-owner"]},{"id":"b248-v15-18-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-monticello","v15s-glen-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「旋渦環流與水頭」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Swirl circulation and head\", which statement holds?","options":["原創教學假設：Circulation=20 m2/s; radius=2 m; tangentialV=20/(2*pi*2)=1.59155 m/s。","靜態單點洩量足以完成任何洪水演算","只達兩倍頻率就保證所有壓力尖峰量測準確"],"optionsEn":["Original teaching assumptions: Circulation=20 m2/s; radius=2 m; tangentialV=20/(2*pi*2)=1.59155 m/s.","One static discharge point is sufficient to route every flood","Sampling at twice the frequency guarantees accurate measurement of every pressure peak"],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創教學假設：Circulation=20 m2/s; radius=2 m; tangentialV=20/(2*pi*2)=1.59155 m/s。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: Circulation=20 m2/s; radius=2 m; tangentialV=20/(2*pi*2)=1.59155 m/s. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":18},{"id":"b248-v15-19","title":"旋渦環流與水頭：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Swirl circulation and head: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-monticello","v15s-glen-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b248-v15-18"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「旋渦環流與水頭」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Swirl circulation and head” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以表面追蹤與速度量測辨識環流方向和渦核範圍。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「只降低平均入流速度可能仍保留強烈環流」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Track the surface and measure velocities to identify circulation and core extent. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: Reducing mean approach speed alone may leave strong circulation. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：交接時以以表面追蹤與速度量測辨識環流方向和渦核範圍作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對只降低平均入流速度可能仍保留強烈環流，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","observationEn":"Site practice: At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Track the surface and measure velocities to identify circulation and core extent. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: Reducing mean approach speed alone may leave strong circulation. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","failure":"注意干擾：只降低平均入流速度可能仍保留強烈環流。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Reducing mean approach speed alone may leave strong circulation. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b248-v15-19-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以表面追蹤與速度量測辨識環流方向和渦核範圍。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「只降低平均入流速度可能仍保留強烈環流」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。","textEn":"Track the surface and measure velocities to identify circulation and core extent. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: Reducing mean approach speed alone may leave strong circulation. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-monticello","v15s-glen-owner"]},{"id":"b248-v15-19-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"交接時以以表面追蹤與速度量測辨識環流方向和渦核範圍作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對只降低平均入流速度可能仍保留強烈環流，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","textEn":"At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Track the surface and measure velocities to identify circulation and core extent. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: Reducing mean approach speed alone may leave strong circulation. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-monticello","v15s-glen-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「旋渦環流與水頭」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Swirl circulation and head\"?","options":["允收準則可以等看到量測數據後再決定。","以表面追蹤與速度量測辨識環流方向和渦核範圍。","孔口控制的流量仍必定與水頭一點五次方成正比"],"optionsEn":["Acceptance criteria can be decided after the measured data have been seen.","Track the surface and measure velocities to identify circulation and core extent.","Orifice discharge must remain proportional to head to the three-halves power"],"answer":1,"explanation":"以表面追蹤與速度量測辨識環流方向和渦核範圍。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Track the surface and measure velocities to identify circulation and core extent. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":19},{"id":"b248-v15-20","title":"旋渦環流與水頭：失效診斷","titleEn":"Swirl circulation and head: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-monticello","v15s-glen-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b248-v15-19"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「旋渦環流與水頭」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Swirl circulation and head” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"只降低平均入流速度可能仍保留強烈環流。診斷時應採取以下查核：以表面追蹤與速度量測辨識環流方向和渦核範圍，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Reducing mean approach speed alone may leave strong circulation. Diagnose it by the following check: Track the surface and measure velocities to identify circulation and core extent. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「平均入流速度低就不可能形成進水旋渦」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Low mean approach speed makes inlet vortices impossible\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b248-v15-20-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"只降低平均入流速度可能仍保留強烈環流。診斷時應採取以下查核：以表面追蹤與速度量測辨識環流方向和渦核範圍，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。","textEn":"Reducing mean approach speed alone may leave strong circulation. Diagnose it by the following check: Track the surface and measure velocities to identify circulation and core extent. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-monticello","v15s-glen-owner"]},{"id":"b248-v15-20-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-monticello","v15s-glen-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「旋渦環流與水頭」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Swirl circulation and head\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["症狀相同就代表原因相同，不必用量測區分。","動量變化單項就是井底彎道全部荷載","只降低平均入流速度可能仍保留強烈環流。"],"optionsEn":["Identical symptoms always mean identical causes, so no discriminating measurement is needed.","Momentum change alone equals the entire bottom-bend load","Reducing mean approach speed alone may leave strong circulation."],"answer":2,"explanation":"只降低平均入流速度可能仍保留強烈環流。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Reducing mean approach speed alone may leave strong circulation. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":20},{"id":"b248-v15-21","title":"豎井底彎轉動量：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Bottom bend momentum change: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-monticello","v15s-glen-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b248-v15-20"],"objective":"說明「豎井底彎轉動量」如何影響豎井式溢洪道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Bottom bend momentum change” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Shaft spillways”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"落水在井底彎轉為水平流時，方向改變形成明顯作用力，壓力與速度沿彎道分布不均。簡化等速直角轉彎的向量差只計動量項，實際支承作用還含壓力力與水重；不可直接把此單項當成彎道完整設計荷載。 驗證時應以彎道壓力積分及入口出口速度向量核對受力方向，並辨識以下失效情境：漏列壓力力會使支承反力估算不完整。這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「豎井底彎轉動量」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"At the shaft bottom, flow turns from vertical to horizontal and generates substantial reaction. An equal-speed right-angle vector difference estimates only momentum change. Real support loads also include pressure forces and water weight, so that single component is not the complete bend design load. Test this interpretation with the following evidence: Check force direction using bend-pressure integration and inlet-outlet velocity vectors. In particular, distinguish this failure mechanism: Omitting pressure forces leaves the support-reaction estimate incomplete. That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Bottom bend momentum change” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：rho=1000 kg/m3; Q=60 m3/s; V=10 m/s; rightAngleMomentumMagnitude=sqrt(2)*1000*60*10/1000=848.528 kN。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: rho=1000 kg/m3; Q=60 m3/s; V=10 m/s; rightAngleMomentumMagnitude=sqrt(2)*1000*60*10/1000=848.528 kN.","failure":"常見誤解：「動量變化單項就是井底彎道全部荷載」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Momentum change alone equals the entire bottom-bend load\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「豎井底彎轉動量」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Bottom bend momentum change”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b248-v15-21-k1","title":"豎井底彎轉動量","titleEn":"Bottom bend momentum change","text":"落水在井底彎轉為水平流時，方向改變形成明顯作用力，壓力與速度沿彎道分布不均。簡化等速直角轉彎的向量差只計動量項，實際支承作用還含壓力力與水重；不可直接把此單項當成彎道完整設計荷載。","textEn":"At the shaft bottom, flow turns from vertical to horizontal and generates substantial reaction. An equal-speed right-angle vector difference estimates only momentum change.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-monticello","v15s-glen-owner"]},{"id":"b248-v15-21-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：動量變化單項就是井底彎道全部荷載 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Momentum change alone equals the entire bottom-bend load Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-monticello","v15s-glen-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「豎井底彎轉動量」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Bottom bend momentum change\" is correct?","options":["落水在井底彎轉為水平流時，方向改變形成明顯作用力，壓力與速度沿彎道分布不均。","動量變化單項就是井底彎道全部荷載","下游管徑夠大就可以忽略全部摩阻"],"optionsEn":["At the shaft bottom, flow turns from vertical to horizontal and generates substantial reaction.","Momentum change alone equals the entire bottom-bend load","A sufficiently large downstream pipe permits ignoring all friction losses"],"answer":0,"explanation":"落水在井底彎轉為水平流時，方向改變形成明顯作用力，壓力與速度沿彎道分布不均。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"At the shaft bottom, flow turns from vertical to horizontal and generates substantial reaction. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":21},{"id":"b248-v15-22","title":"豎井底彎轉動量：定量估算","titleEn":"Bottom bend momentum change: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-monticello","v15s-glen-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b248-v15-21"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「豎井底彎轉動量」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Bottom bend momentum change” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：rho=1000 kg/m3; Q=60 m3/s; V=10 m/s; rightAngleMomentumMagnitude=sqrt(2)*1000*60*10/1000=848.528 kN。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: rho=1000 kg/m3; Q=60 m3/s; V=10 m/s; rightAngleMomentumMagnitude=sqrt(2)*1000*60*10/1000=848.528 kN. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以彎道壓力積分及入口出口速度向量核對受力方向。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Check force direction using bend-pressure integration and inlet-outlet velocity vectors.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b248-v15-22-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：rho=1000 kg/m3; Q=60 m3/s; V=10 m/s; rightAngleMomentumMagnitude=sqrt(2)*1000*60*10/1000=848.528 kN。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: rho=1000 kg/m3; Q=60 m3/s; V=10 m/s; rightAngleMomentumMagnitude=sqrt(2)*1000*60*10/1000=848.528 kN. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-monticello","v15s-glen-owner"]},{"id":"b248-v15-22-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-monticello","v15s-glen-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「豎井底彎轉動量」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Bottom bend momentum change\", which statement holds?","options":["堵塞面積減少三成就保證洩量只減三成","原創教學假設：rho=1000 kg/m3; Q=60 m3/s; V=10 m/s; rightAngleMomentumMagnitude=sqrt(2)*1000*60*10/1000=848.528 kN。","環形堰率定可以延伸到任何高水頭工況"],"optionsEn":["A thirty-percent area blockage guarantees exactly thirty-percent discharge loss","Original teaching assumptions: rho=1000 kg/m3; Q=60 m3/s; V=10 m/s; rightAngleMomentumMagnitude=sqrt(2)*1000*60*10/1000=848.528 kN.","A circular-weir rating remains valid at every high-head condition"],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創教學假設：rho=1000 kg/m3; Q=60 m3/s; V=10 m/s; rightAngleMomentumMagnitude=sqrt(2)*1000*60*10/1000=848.528 kN。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: rho=1000 kg/m3; Q=60 m3/s; V=10 m/s; rightAngleMomentumMagnitude=sqrt(2)*1000*60*10/1000=848.528 kN. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":22},{"id":"b248-v15-23","title":"豎井底彎轉動量：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Bottom bend momentum change: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-monticello","v15s-glen-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b248-v15-22"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「豎井底彎轉動量」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Bottom bend momentum change” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以彎道壓力積分及入口出口速度向量核對受力方向。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「漏列壓力力會使支承反力估算不完整」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Check force direction using bend-pressure integration and inlet-outlet velocity vectors. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: Omitting pressure forces leaves the support-reaction estimate incomplete. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：交接時以以彎道壓力積分及入口出口速度向量核對受力方向作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對漏列壓力力會使支承反力估算不完整，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","observationEn":"Site practice: At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Check force direction using bend-pressure integration and inlet-outlet velocity vectors. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: Omitting pressure forces leaves the support-reaction estimate incomplete. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","failure":"注意干擾：漏列壓力力會使支承反力估算不完整。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Omitting pressure forces leaves the support-reaction estimate incomplete. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b248-v15-23-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以彎道壓力積分及入口出口速度向量核對受力方向。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「漏列壓力力會使支承反力估算不完整」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。","textEn":"Check force direction using bend-pressure integration and inlet-outlet velocity vectors. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: Omitting pressure forces leaves the support-reaction estimate incomplete. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-monticello","v15s-glen-owner"]},{"id":"b248-v15-23-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"交接時以以彎道壓力積分及入口出口速度向量核對受力方向作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對漏列壓力力會使支承反力估算不完整，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","textEn":"At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Check force direction using bend-pressure integration and inlet-outlet velocity vectors. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: Omitting pressure forces leaves the support-reaction estimate incomplete. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-monticello","v15s-glen-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「豎井底彎轉動量」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Bottom bend momentum change\"?","options":["只要結構分析模型看起來合理，就可以省略現場量測與試驗。","整個豎井截面在所有工況都充滿液態水","以彎道壓力積分及入口出口速度向量核對受力方向。"],"optionsEn":["If the structural model looks reasonable, site measurement and testing can be skipped.","The entire shaft section contains liquid water in every operating regime","Check force direction using bend-pressure integration and inlet-outlet velocity vectors."],"answer":2,"explanation":"以彎道壓力積分及入口出口速度向量核對受力方向。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Check force direction using bend-pressure integration and inlet-outlet velocity vectors. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":23},{"id":"b248-v15-24","title":"豎井底彎轉動量：失效診斷","titleEn":"Bottom bend momentum change: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-monticello","v15s-glen-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b248-v15-23"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「豎井底彎轉動量」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Bottom bend momentum change” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"漏列壓力力會使支承反力估算不完整。診斷時應採取以下查核：以彎道壓力積分及入口出口速度向量核對受力方向，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Omitting pressure forces leaves the support-reaction estimate incomplete. Diagnose it by the following check: Check force direction using bend-pressure integration and inlet-outlet velocity vectors. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「動量變化單項就是井底彎道全部荷載」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Momentum change alone equals the entire bottom-bend load\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b248-v15-24-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"漏列壓力力會使支承反力估算不完整。診斷時應採取以下查核：以彎道壓力積分及入口出口速度向量核對受力方向，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。","textEn":"Omitting pressure forces leaves the support-reaction estimate incomplete. Diagnose it by the following check: Check force direction using bend-pressure integration and inlet-outlet velocity vectors. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-monticello","v15s-glen-owner"]},{"id":"b248-v15-24-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-monticello","v15s-glen-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「豎井底彎轉動量」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Bottom bend momentum change\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["漏列壓力力會使支承反力估算不完整。","只要結構還沒倒，就代表安全餘裕仍然足夠。","下游管徑夠大就可以忽略全部摩阻"],"optionsEn":["Omitting pressure forces leaves the support-reaction estimate incomplete.","As long as the structure is still standing, its safety margin must still be adequate.","A sufficiently large downstream pipe permits ignoring all friction losses"],"answer":0,"explanation":"漏列壓力力會使支承反力估算不完整。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Omitting pressure forces leaves the support-reaction estimate incomplete. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":24}],"order":3},{"id":"b248-v15-s4","title":"試驗、量測與監測驗證","titleEn":"Testing, measurement and monitoring","description":"本階段聚焦「下游管流摩阻」與「控制轉換與庫容」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Downstream conduit friction\" and \"Control transition and reservoir storage\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b248-v15-25","title":"下游管流摩阻：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Downstream conduit friction: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-monticello","v15s-glen-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b248-v15-24"],"objective":"說明「下游管流摩阻」如何影響豎井式溢洪道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Downstream conduit friction” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Shaft spillways”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"當下游通道滿流時，沿程摩阻消耗水頭並可能回控豎井容量；自由水面流則需不同計算架構。達西摩阻係數與管長徑比必須配套使用，接頭、彎道與出入口損失另列，不能因管徑大就忽略整段水頭需求。 驗證時應以沿管壓力測點核對摩阻坡降並辨認是否滿流，並辨識以下失效情境：在明滿流交替時套單一穩態管流式會漏掉壓力跳動。這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「下游管流摩阻」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"A full downstream conduit loses head to friction and may control shaft capacity; free-surface operation needs another framework. Use Darcy friction factor consistently with length-to-diameter ratio and list local losses separately. A large diameter does not eliminate the head demand along a long conduit. Test this interpretation with the following evidence: Use pressure taps to check friction gradient and establish whether the conduit is full. In particular, distinguish this failure mechanism: One steady pipe-flow formula misses pressure changes during mixed free-surface and full flow. That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Downstream conduit friction” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：Full pipe: DarcyF=0.018; L=300 m; D=4 m; V=8 m/s; headLoss=0.018*(300/4)*8**2/(2*9.81)=4.40367 m。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: Full pipe: DarcyF=0.018; L=300 m; D=4 m; V=8 m/s; headLoss=0.018*(300/4)*8**2/(2*9.81)=4.40367 m.","failure":"常見誤解：「下游管徑夠大就可以忽略全部摩阻」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A sufficiently large downstream pipe permits ignoring all friction losses\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「下游管流摩阻」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Downstream conduit friction”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b248-v15-25-k1","title":"下游管流摩阻","titleEn":"Downstream conduit friction","text":"當下游通道滿流時，沿程摩阻消耗水頭並可能回控豎井容量；自由水面流則需不同計算架構。達西摩阻係數與管長徑比必須配套使用，接頭、彎道與出入口損失另列，不能因管徑大就忽略整段水頭需求。","textEn":"A full downstream conduit loses head to friction and may control shaft capacity; free-surface operation needs another framework. Use Darcy friction factor consistently with length-to-diameter ratio and list local losses separately.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-monticello","v15s-glen-owner"]},{"id":"b248-v15-25-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：下游管徑夠大就可以忽略全部摩阻 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A sufficiently large downstream pipe permits ignoring all friction losses Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-monticello","v15s-glen-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「下游管流摩阻」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Downstream conduit friction\" is correct?","options":["下游管徑夠大就可以忽略全部摩阻","當下游通道滿流時，沿程摩阻消耗水頭並可能回控豎井容量；自由水面流則需不同計算架構。","靜態單點洩量足以完成任何洪水演算"],"optionsEn":["A sufficiently large downstream pipe permits ignoring all friction losses","A full downstream conduit loses head to friction and may control shaft capacity; free-surface operation needs another framework.","One static discharge point is sufficient to route every flood"],"answer":1,"explanation":"當下游通道滿流時，沿程摩阻消耗水頭並可能回控豎井容量；自由水面流則需不同計算架構。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"A full downstream conduit loses head to friction and may control shaft capacity; free-surface operation needs another framework. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":25},{"id":"b248-v15-26","title":"下游管流摩阻：定量估算","titleEn":"Downstream conduit friction: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-monticello","v15s-glen-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b248-v15-25"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「下游管流摩阻」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Downstream conduit friction” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：Full pipe: DarcyF=0.018; L=300 m; D=4 m; V=8 m/s; headLoss=0.018*(300/4)*8**2/(2*9.81)=4.40367 m。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: Full pipe: DarcyF=0.018; L=300 m; D=4 m; V=8 m/s; headLoss=0.018*(300/4)*8**2/(2*9.81)=4.40367 m. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以沿管壓力測點核對摩阻坡降並辨認是否滿流。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Use pressure taps to check friction gradient and establish whether the conduit is full.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b248-v15-26-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：Full pipe: DarcyF=0.018; L=300 m; D=4 m; V=8 m/s; headLoss=0.018*(300/4)*8**2/(2*9.81)=4.40367 m。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: Full pipe: DarcyF=0.018; L=300 m; D=4 m; V=8 m/s; headLoss=0.018*(300/4)*8**2/(2*9.81)=4.40367 m. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-monticello","v15s-glen-owner"]},{"id":"b248-v15-26-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-monticello","v15s-glen-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「下游管流摩阻」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Downstream conduit friction\", which statement holds?","options":["只達兩倍頻率就保證所有壓力尖峰量測準確","孔口控制的流量仍必定與水頭一點五次方成正比","原創教學假設：Full pipe: DarcyF=0.018; L=300 m; D=4 m; V=8 m/s; headLoss=0.018*(300/4)*8**2/(2*9.81)=4.40367 m。"],"optionsEn":["Sampling at twice the frequency guarantees accurate measurement of every pressure peak","Orifice discharge must remain proportional to head to the three-halves power","Original teaching assumptions: Full pipe: DarcyF=0.018; L=300 m; D=4 m; V=8 m/s; headLoss=0.018*(300/4)*8**2/(2*9.81)=4.40367 m."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設：Full pipe: DarcyF=0.018; L=300 m; D=4 m; V=8 m/s; headLoss=0.018*(300/4)*8**2/(2*9.81)=4.40367 m。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: Full pipe: DarcyF=0.018; L=300 m; D=4 m; V=8 m/s; headLoss=0.018*(300/4)*8**2/(2*9.81)=4.40367 m. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":26},{"id":"b248-v15-27","title":"下游管流摩阻：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Downstream conduit friction: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-monticello","v15s-glen-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b248-v15-26"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「下游管流摩阻」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Downstream conduit friction” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以沿管壓力測點核對摩阻坡降並辨認是否滿流。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「在明滿流交替時套單一穩態管流式會漏掉壓力跳動」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Use pressure taps to check friction gradient and establish whether the conduit is full. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: One steady pipe-flow formula misses pressure changes during mixed free-surface and full flow. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：交接時以以沿管壓力測點核對摩阻坡降並辨認是否滿流作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對在明滿流交替時套單一穩態管流式會漏掉壓力跳動，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","observationEn":"Site practice: At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Use pressure taps to check friction gradient and establish whether the conduit is full. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: One steady pipe-flow formula misses pressure changes during mixed free-surface and full flow. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","failure":"注意干擾：在明滿流交替時套單一穩態管流式會漏掉壓力跳動。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: One steady pipe-flow formula misses pressure changes during mixed free-surface and full flow. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b248-v15-27-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以沿管壓力測點核對摩阻坡降並辨認是否滿流。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「在明滿流交替時套單一穩態管流式會漏掉壓力跳動」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。","textEn":"Use pressure taps to check friction gradient and establish whether the conduit is full. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: One steady pipe-flow formula misses pressure changes during mixed free-surface and full flow. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-monticello","v15s-glen-owner"]},{"id":"b248-v15-27-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"交接時以以沿管壓力測點核對摩阻坡降並辨認是否滿流作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對在明滿流交替時套單一穩態管流式會漏掉壓力跳動，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","textEn":"At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Use pressure taps to check friction gradient and establish whether the conduit is full. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: One steady pipe-flow formula misses pressure changes during mixed free-surface and full flow. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-monticello","v15s-glen-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「下游管流摩阻」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Downstream conduit friction\"?","options":["以沿管壓力測點核對摩阻坡降並辨認是否滿流。","量測時不必記錄溫度、水頭、水位歷程與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","通氣管存在就保證任何流量下都能充分補氣"],"optionsEn":["Use pressure taps to check friction gradient and establish whether the conduit is full.","Temperature, water head, water-level history and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","A vent pipe guarantees adequate air supply at every water discharge"],"answer":0,"explanation":"以沿管壓力測點核對摩阻坡降並辨認是否滿流。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Use pressure taps to check friction gradient and establish whether the conduit is full. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":27},{"id":"b248-v15-28","title":"下游管流摩阻：失效診斷","titleEn":"Downstream conduit friction: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-monticello","v15s-glen-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b248-v15-27"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「下游管流摩阻」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Downstream conduit friction” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"在明滿流交替時套單一穩態管流式會漏掉壓力跳動。診斷時應採取以下查核：以沿管壓力測點核對摩阻坡降並辨認是否滿流，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"One steady pipe-flow formula misses pressure changes during mixed free-surface and full flow. Diagnose it by the following check: Use pressure taps to check friction gradient and establish whether the conduit is full. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「下游管徑夠大就可以忽略全部摩阻」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A sufficiently large downstream pipe permits ignoring all friction losses\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b248-v15-28-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"在明滿流交替時套單一穩態管流式會漏掉壓力跳動。診斷時應採取以下查核：以沿管壓力測點核對摩阻坡降並辨認是否滿流，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。","textEn":"One steady pipe-flow formula misses pressure changes during mixed free-surface and full flow. Diagnose it by the following check: Use pressure taps to check friction gradient and establish whether the conduit is full. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-monticello","v15s-glen-owner"]},{"id":"b248-v15-28-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-monticello","v15s-glen-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「下游管流摩阻」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Downstream conduit friction\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","在明滿流交替時套單一穩態管流式會漏掉壓力跳動。","靜態單點洩量足以完成任何洪水演算"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","One steady pipe-flow formula misses pressure changes during mixed free-surface and full flow.","One static discharge point is sufficient to route every flood"],"answer":1,"explanation":"在明滿流交替時套單一穩態管流式會漏掉壓力跳動。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"One steady pipe-flow formula misses pressure changes during mixed free-surface and full flow. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":28},{"id":"b248-v15-29","title":"控制轉換與庫容：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Control transition and reservoir storage: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-monticello","v15s-glen-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b248-v15-28"],"objective":"說明「控制轉換與庫容」如何影響豎井式溢洪道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Control transition and reservoir storage” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Shaft spillways”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"豎井洩量率定的斜率變小時，新增入流可能更多轉為庫水位上升，應把水庫蓄水方程與溢洪道控制連接。定面積短時近似只表示水量差，不含變動庫容曲線與時間相依洩量；完整洪水演算不能靠單一靜態率定點。 驗證時應用同時入出流與水位量測核對庫容變化並檢查率定斜率，並辨識以下失效情境：延用自由堰流高斜率會低估轉換後水位上升。這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「控制轉換與庫容」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"When the discharge-rating slope decreases, more incoming water may become reservoir storage. Couple continuity to the spillway control relation. A constant-area short-interval estimate illustrates imbalance but omits changing storage geometry and time-dependent outflow; one static rating point cannot route a flood. Test this interpretation with the following evidence: Reconcile simultaneous inflow, outflow and stage change and inspect rating-curve slope. In particular, distinguish this failure mechanism: Extending the steep free-weir rating understates stage rise after control changes. That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Control transition and reservoir storage” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：Inflow=150 m3/s; outflow=110 m3/s; interval=600 s; reservoirArea=2000000 m2; stageRise=(150-110)*600/2000000=0.012 m。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: Inflow=150 m3/s; outflow=110 m3/s; interval=600 s; reservoirArea=2000000 m2; stageRise=(150-110)*600/2000000=0.012 m.","failure":"常見誤解：「靜態單點洩量足以完成任何洪水演算」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"One static discharge point is sufficient to route every flood\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「控制轉換與庫容」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Control transition and reservoir storage”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b248-v15-29-k1","title":"控制轉換與庫容","titleEn":"Control transition and reservoir storage","text":"豎井洩量率定的斜率變小時，新增入流可能更多轉為庫水位上升，應把水庫蓄水方程與溢洪道控制連接。定面積短時近似只表示水量差，不含變動庫容曲線與時間相依洩量；完整洪水演算不能靠單一靜態率定點。","textEn":"When the discharge-rating slope decreases, more incoming water may become reservoir storage. Couple continuity to the spillway control relation.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-monticello","v15s-glen-owner"]},{"id":"b248-v15-29-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：靜態單點洩量足以完成任何洪水演算 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: One static discharge point is sufficient to route every flood Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-monticello","v15s-glen-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「控制轉換與庫容」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Control transition and reservoir storage\" is correct?","options":["靜態單點洩量足以完成任何洪水演算","堵塞面積減少三成就保證洩量只減三成","豎井洩量率定的斜率變小時，新增入流可能更多轉為庫水位上升，應把水庫蓄水方程與溢洪道控制連接。"],"optionsEn":["One static discharge point is sufficient to route every flood","A thirty-percent area blockage guarantees exactly thirty-percent discharge loss","When the discharge-rating slope decreases, more incoming water may become reservoir storage."],"answer":2,"explanation":"豎井洩量率定的斜率變小時，新增入流可能更多轉為庫水位上升，應把水庫蓄水方程與溢洪道控制連接。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"When the discharge-rating slope decreases, more incoming water may become reservoir storage. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":29},{"id":"b248-v15-30","title":"控制轉換與庫容：定量估算","titleEn":"Control transition and reservoir storage: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-monticello","v15s-glen-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b248-v15-29"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「控制轉換與庫容」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Control transition and reservoir storage” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：Inflow=150 m3/s; outflow=110 m3/s; interval=600 s; reservoirArea=2000000 m2; stageRise=(150-110)*600/2000000=0.012 m。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: Inflow=150 m3/s; outflow=110 m3/s; interval=600 s; reservoirArea=2000000 m2; stageRise=(150-110)*600/2000000=0.012 m. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：用同時入出流與水位量測核對庫容變化並檢查率定斜率。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Reconcile simultaneous inflow, outflow and stage change and inspect rating-curve slope.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b248-v15-30-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：Inflow=150 m3/s; outflow=110 m3/s; interval=600 s; reservoirArea=2000000 m2; stageRise=(150-110)*600/2000000=0.012 m。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: Inflow=150 m3/s; outflow=110 m3/s; interval=600 s; reservoirArea=2000000 m2; stageRise=(150-110)*600/2000000=0.012 m. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-monticello","v15s-glen-owner"]},{"id":"b248-v15-30-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-monticello","v15s-glen-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「控制轉換與庫容」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Control transition and reservoir storage\", which statement holds?","options":["原創教學假設：Inflow=150 m3/s; outflow=110 m3/s; interval=600 s; reservoirArea=2000000 m2; stageRise=(150-110)*600/2000000=0.012 m。","環形堰率定可以延伸到任何高水頭工況","整個豎井截面在所有工況都充滿液態水"],"optionsEn":["Original teaching assumptions: Inflow=150 m3/s; outflow=110 m3/s; interval=600 s; reservoirArea=2000000 m2; stageRise=(150-110)*600/2000000=0.012 m.","A circular-weir rating remains valid at every high-head condition","The entire shaft section contains liquid water in every operating regime"],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創教學假設：Inflow=150 m3/s; outflow=110 m3/s; interval=600 s; reservoirArea=2000000 m2; stageRise=(150-110)*600/2000000=0.012 m。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: Inflow=150 m3/s; outflow=110 m3/s; interval=600 s; reservoirArea=2000000 m2; stageRise=(150-110)*600/2000000=0.012 m. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":30},{"id":"b248-v15-31","title":"控制轉換與庫容：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Control transition and reservoir storage: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-monticello","v15s-glen-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b248-v15-30"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「控制轉換與庫容」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Control transition and reservoir storage” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"用同時入出流與水位量測核對庫容變化並檢查率定斜率。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「延用自由堰流高斜率會低估轉換後水位上升」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Reconcile simultaneous inflow, outflow and stage change and inspect rating-curve slope. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: Extending the steep free-weir rating understates stage rise after control changes. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：交接時以用同時入出流與水位量測核對庫容變化並檢查率定斜率作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對延用自由堰流高斜率會低估轉換後水位上升，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","observationEn":"Site practice: At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Reconcile simultaneous inflow, outflow and stage change and inspect rating-curve slope. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: Extending the steep free-weir rating understates stage rise after control changes. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","failure":"注意干擾：延用自由堰流高斜率會低估轉換後水位上升。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Extending the steep free-weir rating understates stage rise after control changes. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b248-v15-31-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"用同時入出流與水位量測核對庫容變化並檢查率定斜率。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「延用自由堰流高斜率會低估轉換後水位上升」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。","textEn":"Reconcile simultaneous inflow, outflow and stage change and inspect rating-curve slope. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: Extending the steep free-weir rating understates stage rise after control changes. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-monticello","v15s-glen-owner"]},{"id":"b248-v15-31-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"交接時以用同時入出流與水位量測核對庫容變化並檢查率定斜率作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對延用自由堰流高斜率會低估轉換後水位上升，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","textEn":"At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Reconcile simultaneous inflow, outflow and stage change and inspect rating-curve slope. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: Extending the steep free-weir rating understates stage rise after control changes. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-monticello","v15s-glen-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「控制轉換與庫容」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Control transition and reservoir storage\"?","options":["沿用另一處水工設施或流域的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","用同時入出流與水位量測核對庫容變化並檢查率定斜率。","平均入流速度低就不可能形成進水旋渦"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another hydraulic structure or catchment counts as verifying this structure.","Reconcile simultaneous inflow, outflow and stage change and inspect rating-curve slope.","Low mean approach speed makes inlet vortices impossible"],"answer":1,"explanation":"用同時入出流與水位量測核對庫容變化並檢查率定斜率。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Reconcile simultaneous inflow, outflow and stage change and inspect rating-curve slope. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":31},{"id":"b248-v15-32","title":"控制轉換與庫容：失效診斷","titleEn":"Control transition and reservoir storage: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-monticello","v15s-glen-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b248-v15-31"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「控制轉換與庫容」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Control transition and reservoir storage” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"延用自由堰流高斜率會低估轉換後水位上升。診斷時應採取以下查核：用同時入出流與水位量測核對庫容變化並檢查率定斜率，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Extending the steep free-weir rating understates stage rise after control changes. Diagnose it by the following check: Reconcile simultaneous inflow, outflow and stage change and inspect rating-curve slope. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「靜態單點洩量足以完成任何洪水演算」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"One static discharge point is sufficient to route every flood\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b248-v15-32-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"延用自由堰流高斜率會低估轉換後水位上升。診斷時應採取以下查核：用同時入出流與水位量測核對庫容變化並檢查率定斜率，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。","textEn":"Extending the steep free-weir rating understates stage rise after control changes. Diagnose it by the following check: Reconcile simultaneous inflow, outflow and stage change and inspect rating-curve slope. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-monticello","v15s-glen-owner"]},{"id":"b248-v15-32-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-monticello","v15s-glen-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「控制轉換與庫容」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Control transition and reservoir storage\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","堵塞面積減少三成就保證洩量只減三成","延用自由堰流高斜率會低估轉換後水位上升。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","A thirty-percent area blockage guarantees exactly thirty-percent discharge loss","Extending the steep free-weir rating understates stage rise after control changes."],"answer":2,"explanation":"延用自由堰流高斜率會低估轉換後水位上升。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Extending the steep free-weir rating understates stage rise after control changes. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":32}],"order":4},{"id":"b248-v15-s5","title":"耐久、維護與工程交接","titleEn":"Durability, maintenance and engineering handoff","description":"本階段聚焦「漂流物與局部堵塞」與「瞬變量測與取樣」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Floating debris and local blockage\" and \"Transient measurement and sampling\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b248-v15-33","title":"漂流物與局部堵塞：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Floating debris and local blockage: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-monticello","v15s-glen-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b248-v15-32"],"objective":"說明「漂流物與局部堵塞」如何影響豎井式溢洪道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Floating debris and local blockage” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Shaft spillways”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"鐘口附近漂流物可形成環狀或偏心堵塞，既減少有效入口又引入不對稱旋流。單純面積減量只作幾何示意，實際洩量還受堆積形狀與通氣影響；試驗需涵蓋不同漂流物位置以及清除前後的水位反應。 驗證時應以多種堵塞布置觀察偏流旋渦與通氣壓力變化，並辨識以下失效情境：偏心堵塞可能同時削弱洩量與補氣。這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「漂流物與局部堵塞」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Debris around a bellmouth can block the inlet asymmetrically and induce swirl. An area deduction describes geometry only; discharge also depends on accumulation shape and ventilation. Test different positions and examine stage response before and after removal instead of equating blockage area with discharge loss. Test this interpretation with the following evidence: Observe asymmetric flow, vortices and ventilation pressures for several blockage layouts. In particular, distinguish this failure mechanism: Eccentric blockage may reduce both discharge and ventilation. That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Floating debris and local blockage” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：NominalOpenArea=20 m2; blockedArea=6 m2; openFraction=(20-6)/20=0.70。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: NominalOpenArea=20 m2; blockedArea=6 m2; openFraction=(20-6)/20=0.70.","failure":"常見誤解：「堵塞面積減少三成就保證洩量只減三成」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A thirty-percent area blockage guarantees exactly thirty-percent discharge loss\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「漂流物與局部堵塞」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Floating debris and local blockage”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b248-v15-33-k1","title":"漂流物與局部堵塞","titleEn":"Floating debris and local blockage","text":"鐘口附近漂流物可形成環狀或偏心堵塞，既減少有效入口又引入不對稱旋流。單純面積減量只作幾何示意，實際洩量還受堆積形狀與通氣影響；試驗需涵蓋不同漂流物位置以及清除前後的水位反應。","textEn":"Debris around a bellmouth can block the inlet asymmetrically and induce swirl. An area deduction describes geometry only; discharge also depends on accumulation shape and ventilation.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-monticello","v15s-glen-owner"]},{"id":"b248-v15-33-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：堵塞面積減少三成就保證洩量只減三成 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A thirty-percent area blockage guarantees exactly thirty-percent discharge loss Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-monticello","v15s-glen-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「漂流物與局部堵塞」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Floating debris and local blockage\" is correct?","options":["鐘口附近漂流物可形成環狀或偏心堵塞，既減少有效入口又引入不對稱旋流。","堵塞面積減少三成就保證洩量只減三成","只達兩倍頻率就保證所有壓力尖峰量測準確"],"optionsEn":["Debris around a bellmouth can block the inlet asymmetrically and induce swirl.","A thirty-percent area blockage guarantees exactly thirty-percent discharge loss","Sampling at twice the frequency guarantees accurate measurement of every pressure peak"],"answer":0,"explanation":"鐘口附近漂流物可形成環狀或偏心堵塞，既減少有效入口又引入不對稱旋流。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Debris around a bellmouth can block the inlet asymmetrically and induce swirl. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":33},{"id":"b248-v15-34","title":"漂流物與局部堵塞：定量估算","titleEn":"Floating debris and local blockage: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-monticello","v15s-glen-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b248-v15-33"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「漂流物與局部堵塞」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Floating debris and local blockage” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：NominalOpenArea=20 m2; blockedArea=6 m2; openFraction=(20-6)/20=0.70。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: NominalOpenArea=20 m2; blockedArea=6 m2; openFraction=(20-6)/20=0.70. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以多種堵塞布置觀察偏流旋渦與通氣壓力變化。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Observe asymmetric flow, vortices and ventilation pressures for several blockage layouts.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b248-v15-34-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：NominalOpenArea=20 m2; blockedArea=6 m2; openFraction=(20-6)/20=0.70。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: NominalOpenArea=20 m2; blockedArea=6 m2; openFraction=(20-6)/20=0.70. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-monticello","v15s-glen-owner"]},{"id":"b248-v15-34-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-monticello","v15s-glen-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「漂流物與局部堵塞」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Floating debris and local blockage\", which statement holds?","options":["孔口控制的流量仍必定與水頭一點五次方成正比","原創教學假設：NominalOpenArea=20 m2; blockedArea=6 m2; openFraction=(20-6)/20=0.70。","通氣管存在就保證任何流量下都能充分補氣"],"optionsEn":["Orifice discharge must remain proportional to head to the three-halves power","Original teaching assumptions: NominalOpenArea=20 m2; blockedArea=6 m2; openFraction=(20-6)/20=0.70.","A vent pipe guarantees adequate air supply at every water discharge"],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創教學假設：NominalOpenArea=20 m2; blockedArea=6 m2; openFraction=(20-6)/20=0.70。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: NominalOpenArea=20 m2; blockedArea=6 m2; openFraction=(20-6)/20=0.70. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":34},{"id":"b248-v15-35","title":"漂流物與局部堵塞：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Floating debris and local blockage: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-monticello","v15s-glen-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b248-v15-34"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「漂流物與局部堵塞」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Floating debris and local blockage” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以多種堵塞布置觀察偏流旋渦與通氣壓力變化。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「偏心堵塞可能同時削弱洩量與補氣」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Observe asymmetric flow, vortices and ventilation pressures for several blockage layouts. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: Eccentric blockage may reduce both discharge and ventilation. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：交接時以以多種堵塞布置觀察偏流旋渦與通氣壓力變化作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對偏心堵塞可能同時削弱洩量與補氣，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","observationEn":"Site practice: At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Observe asymmetric flow, vortices and ventilation pressures for several blockage layouts. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: Eccentric blockage may reduce both discharge and ventilation. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","failure":"注意干擾：偏心堵塞可能同時削弱洩量與補氣。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Eccentric blockage may reduce both discharge and ventilation. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b248-v15-35-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以多種堵塞布置觀察偏流旋渦與通氣壓力變化。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「偏心堵塞可能同時削弱洩量與補氣」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。","textEn":"Observe asymmetric flow, vortices and ventilation pressures for several blockage layouts. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: Eccentric blockage may reduce both discharge and ventilation. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-monticello","v15s-glen-owner"]},{"id":"b248-v15-35-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"交接時以以多種堵塞布置觀察偏流旋渦與通氣壓力變化作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對偏心堵塞可能同時削弱洩量與補氣，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","textEn":"At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Observe asymmetric flow, vortices and ventilation pressures for several blockage layouts. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: Eccentric blockage may reduce both discharge and ventilation. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-monticello","v15s-glen-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「漂流物與局部堵塞」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Floating debris and local blockage\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","動量變化單項就是井底彎道全部荷載","以多種堵塞布置觀察偏流旋渦與通氣壓力變化。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","Momentum change alone equals the entire bottom-bend load","Observe asymmetric flow, vortices and ventilation pressures for several blockage layouts."],"answer":2,"explanation":"以多種堵塞布置觀察偏流旋渦與通氣壓力變化。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Observe asymmetric flow, vortices and ventilation pressures for several blockage layouts. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":35},{"id":"b248-v15-36","title":"漂流物與局部堵塞：失效診斷","titleEn":"Floating debris and local blockage: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-monticello","v15s-glen-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b248-v15-35"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「漂流物與局部堵塞」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Floating debris and local blockage” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"偏心堵塞可能同時削弱洩量與補氣。診斷時應採取以下查核：以多種堵塞布置觀察偏流旋渦與通氣壓力變化，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Eccentric blockage may reduce both discharge and ventilation. Diagnose it by the following check: Observe asymmetric flow, vortices and ventilation pressures for several blockage layouts. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「堵塞面積減少三成就保證洩量只減三成」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A thirty-percent area blockage guarantees exactly thirty-percent discharge loss\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b248-v15-36-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"偏心堵塞可能同時削弱洩量與補氣。診斷時應採取以下查核：以多種堵塞布置觀察偏流旋渦與通氣壓力變化，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。","textEn":"Eccentric blockage may reduce both discharge and ventilation. Diagnose it by the following check: Observe asymmetric flow, vortices and ventilation pressures for several blockage layouts. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-monticello","v15s-glen-owner"]},{"id":"b248-v15-36-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-monticello","v15s-glen-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「漂流物與局部堵塞」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Floating debris and local blockage\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["偏心堵塞可能同時削弱洩量與補氣。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","只達兩倍頻率就保證所有壓力尖峰量測準確"],"optionsEn":["Eccentric blockage may reduce both discharge and ventilation.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","Sampling at twice the frequency guarantees accurate measurement of every pressure peak"],"answer":0,"explanation":"偏心堵塞可能同時削弱洩量與補氣。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Eccentric blockage may reduce both discharge and ventilation. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":36},{"id":"b248-v15-37","title":"瞬變量測與取樣：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Transient measurement and sampling: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-monticello","v15s-glen-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b248-v15-36"],"objective":"說明「瞬變量測與取樣」如何影響豎井式溢洪道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Transient measurement and sampling” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Shaft spillways”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"控制轉換伴隨的壓力振盪可能比水位平均變化快，量測系統需足夠採樣率並處理抗混疊。奈奎斯特條件只是避免理想頻率折疊的最低要求，不代表波形與尖峰已被精確重建；需根據實際頻帶與感測器響應安排記錄。 驗證時應以較高採樣率對照頻譜並測試感測器動態響應，並辨識以下失效情境：未濾波的高頻振動可能折疊成假低頻壓力週期。這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「瞬變量測與取樣」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Pressure oscillations during control transitions may be faster than mean stage changes. Sampling and anti-alias filtering must cover the relevant band. Nyquist is a minimum ideal condition, not a guarantee of accurate waveform or peak reconstruction; account for the sensor response and observed frequency content. Test this interpretation with the following evidence: Compare spectra at a higher rate and test the pressure sensor dynamic response. In particular, distinguish this failure mechanism: Unfiltered high-frequency vibration can alias into a false low-frequency pressure cycle. That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Transient measurement and sampling” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：HighestIllustrativeFrequency=8 Hz; theoreticalNyquistRate=2*8=16 samples/s; actual acquisition requires additional margin。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: HighestIllustrativeFrequency=8 Hz; theoreticalNyquistRate=2*8=16 samples/s; actual acquisition requires additional margin.","failure":"常見誤解：「只達兩倍頻率就保證所有壓力尖峰量測準確」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Sampling at twice the frequency guarantees accurate measurement of every pressure peak\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「瞬變量測與取樣」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Transient measurement and sampling”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b248-v15-37-k1","title":"瞬變量測與取樣","titleEn":"Transient measurement and sampling","text":"控制轉換伴隨的壓力振盪可能比水位平均變化快，量測系統需足夠採樣率並處理抗混疊。奈奎斯特條件只是避免理想頻率折疊的最低要求，不代表波形與尖峰已被精確重建；需根據實際頻帶與感測器響應安排記錄。","textEn":"Pressure oscillations during control transitions may be faster than mean stage changes. Sampling and anti-alias filtering must cover the relevant band.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-monticello","v15s-glen-owner"]},{"id":"b248-v15-37-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：只達兩倍頻率就保證所有壓力尖峰量測準確 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Sampling at twice the frequency guarantees accurate measurement of every pressure peak Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-monticello","v15s-glen-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「瞬變量測與取樣」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Transient measurement and sampling\" is correct?","options":["只達兩倍頻率就保證所有壓力尖峰量測準確","控制轉換伴隨的壓力振盪可能比水位平均變化快，量測系統需足夠採樣率並處理抗混疊。","環形堰率定可以延伸到任何高水頭工況"],"optionsEn":["Sampling at twice the frequency guarantees accurate measurement of every pressure peak","Pressure oscillations during control transitions may be faster than mean stage changes.","A circular-weir rating remains valid at every high-head condition"],"answer":1,"explanation":"控制轉換伴隨的壓力振盪可能比水位平均變化快，量測系統需足夠採樣率並處理抗混疊。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Pressure oscillations during control transitions may be faster than mean stage changes. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":37},{"id":"b248-v15-38","title":"瞬變量測與取樣：定量估算","titleEn":"Transient measurement and sampling: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-monticello","v15s-glen-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b248-v15-37"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「瞬變量測與取樣」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Transient measurement and sampling” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：HighestIllustrativeFrequency=8 Hz; theoreticalNyquistRate=2*8=16 samples/s; actual acquisition requires additional margin。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: HighestIllustrativeFrequency=8 Hz; theoreticalNyquistRate=2*8=16 samples/s; actual acquisition requires additional margin. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以較高採樣率對照頻譜並測試感測器動態響應。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Compare spectra at a higher rate and test the pressure sensor dynamic response.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b248-v15-38-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：HighestIllustrativeFrequency=8 Hz; theoreticalNyquistRate=2*8=16 samples/s; actual acquisition requires additional margin。數值只檢查量綱與機制，不是實測資料、設計設定或允收門檻。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: HighestIllustrativeFrequency=8 Hz; theoreticalNyquistRate=2*8=16 samples/s; actual acquisition requires additional margin. These values check dimensions and mechanism, not measured data, design settings or acceptance thresholds.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-monticello","v15s-glen-owner"]},{"id":"b248-v15-38-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-monticello","v15s-glen-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「瞬變量測與取樣」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Transient measurement and sampling\", which statement holds?","options":["整個豎井截面在所有工況都充滿液態水","平均入流速度低就不可能形成進水旋渦","原創教學假設：HighestIllustrativeFrequency=8 Hz; theoreticalNyquistRate=2*8=16 samples/s; actual acquisition requires additional margin。"],"optionsEn":["The entire shaft section contains liquid water in every operating regime","Low mean approach speed makes inlet vortices impossible","Original teaching assumptions: HighestIllustrativeFrequency=8 Hz; theoreticalNyquistRate=2*8=16 samples/s; actual acquisition requires additional margin."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設：HighestIllustrativeFrequency=8 Hz; theoreticalNyquistRate=2*8=16 samples/s; actual acquisition requires additional margin。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: HighestIllustrativeFrequency=8 Hz; theoreticalNyquistRate=2*8=16 samples/s; actual acquisition requires additional margin. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":38},{"id":"b248-v15-39","title":"瞬變量測與取樣：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Transient measurement and sampling: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-monticello","v15s-glen-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b248-v15-38"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「瞬變量測與取樣」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Transient measurement and sampling” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以較高採樣率對照頻譜並測試感測器動態響應。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「未濾波的高頻振動可能折疊成假低頻壓力週期」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Compare spectra at a higher rate and test the pressure sensor dynamic response. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: Unfiltered high-frequency vibration can alias into a false low-frequency pressure cycle. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：交接時以以較高採樣率對照頻譜並測試感測器動態響應作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對未濾波的高頻振動可能折疊成假低頻壓力週期，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","observationEn":"Site practice: At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Compare spectra at a higher rate and test the pressure sensor dynamic response. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: Unfiltered high-frequency vibration can alias into a false low-frequency pressure cycle. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","failure":"注意干擾：未濾波的高頻振動可能折疊成假低頻壓力週期。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Unfiltered high-frequency vibration can alias into a false low-frequency pressure cycle. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b248-v15-39-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以較高採樣率對照頻譜並測試感測器動態響應。應將原始量測與本單元模型的輸入條件對齊，並針對「未濾波的高頻振動可能折疊成假低頻壓力週期」取得獨立證據；同時保留儀器校正、測點位置與時間，避免把不同工況的資料直接相減。","textEn":"Compare spectra at a higher rate and test the pressure sensor dynamic response. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: Unfiltered high-frequency vibration can alias into a false low-frequency pressure cycle. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-monticello","v15s-glen-owner"]},{"id":"b248-v15-39-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"交接時以以較高採樣率對照頻譜並測試感測器動態響應作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對未濾波的高頻振動可能折疊成假低頻壓力週期，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。","textEn":"At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Compare spectra at a higher rate and test the pressure sensor dynamic response. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: Unfiltered high-frequency vibration can alias into a false low-frequency pressure cycle. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-monticello","v15s-glen-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「瞬變量測與取樣」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Transient measurement and sampling\"?","options":["以較高採樣率對照頻譜並測試感測器動態響應。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","下游管徑夠大就可以忽略全部摩阻"],"optionsEn":["Compare spectra at a higher rate and test the pressure sensor dynamic response.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","A sufficiently large downstream pipe permits ignoring all friction losses"],"answer":0,"explanation":"以較高採樣率對照頻譜並測試感測器動態響應。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Compare spectra at a higher rate and test the pressure sensor dynamic response. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":39},{"id":"b248-v15-40","title":"瞬變量測與取樣：失效診斷","titleEn":"Transient measurement and sampling: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-monticello","v15s-glen-owner"],"prerequisiteIds":["b248-v15-39"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「瞬變量測與取樣」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Transient measurement and sampling” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"未濾波的高頻振動可能折疊成假低頻壓力週期。診斷時應採取以下查核：以較高採樣率對照頻譜並測試感測器動態響應，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Unfiltered high-frequency vibration can alias into a false low-frequency pressure cycle. Diagnose it by the following check: Compare spectra at a higher rate and test the pressure sensor dynamic response. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「只達兩倍頻率就保證所有壓力尖峰量測準確」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Sampling at twice the frequency guarantees accurate measurement of every pressure peak\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b248-v15-40-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"未濾波的高頻振動可能折疊成假低頻壓力週期。診斷時應採取以下查核：以較高採樣率對照頻譜並測試感測器動態響應，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。","textEn":"Unfiltered high-frequency vibration can alias into a false low-frequency pressure cycle. Diagnose it by the following check: Compare spectra at a higher rate and test the pressure sensor dynamic response. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-monticello","v15s-glen-owner"]},{"id":"b248-v15-40-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-monticello","v15s-glen-owner"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「瞬變量測與取樣」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Transient measurement and sampling\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","未濾波的高頻振動可能折疊成假低頻壓力週期。","環形堰率定可以延伸到任何高水頭工況"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Unfiltered high-frequency vibration can alias into a false low-frequency pressure cycle.","A circular-weir rating remains valid at every high-head condition"],"answer":1,"explanation":"未濾波的高頻振動可能折疊成假低頻壓力週期。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Unfiltered high-frequency vibration can alias into a false low-frequency pressure cycle. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":40}],"order":5}],"sourceIds":["b-src-water-manuals","b-src-water","v15s-usace-spillway","v15s-usbr-monticello","v15s-glen-owner"],"curriculumVersion":15,"stepCount":40,"estimatedMinutes":1000}};
